{
  "dom_id": "step-q97022",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/699e6ce441757dd21b01524b5405ab7f4b596bfe9ec6f8d0532a1e6f112eb8ad.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(1,2)$, $(2,4),$ $(3,6).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/791c82648482ef9932562150659ef74bb55df0216047ad56bb84f9bcf1b6ce4d.png)",
